From 97af8d31d6e0273a1c1b4b84e066a914c00f36fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:37:35 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] daemon: Report client capabilities to the portal

Browsers call isUserVerifyingPlatformAuthenticatorAvailable() and
getClientCapabilities() to decide whether to offer passkey creation.
The portal has no way to answer them from what credentialsd can do, so
it hard-codes the values.

Add GetClientCapabilities() to the handler interface. It returns an
a{sv} of booleans with the WebAuthn client capability names in
snake_case. user_verifying_platform_authenticator is true when a platform
provider answers GetInfo() with at least one user verification method;
a locked provider counts, since the user is asked to unlock it.
passkey_platform_authenticator is true with such a provider or with the
hybrid transport. related_origins reflects that requests are validated
with related origin requests. Conditional mediation and the signal
methods are not supported yet and are reported as false.
